/-! ### merged from `ECDSAAdd.Submission.Entrant.StairMiddleShape_at_Main` -/
section Merge_StairMiddleShape_at_Main

/-!
# The record point-encoding shape of the hosted caller middle

The record program `AboveFieldPointDevelop.programQ` encodes the selected
point with `AboveFieldPointDevelop.encode` / `decode`
(`abbrev`s of `AboveFieldTagDevelop.encode` / `decode`, MainRecord.lean
50541–50542, used by `AboveFieldPointDevelop.middle`, 50687–50688).
CANON 1319's `StairConcreteAssembly.hostedMiddle` instead uses the older
`ControlPointEncodingDevelop.encode` / `decode` (MainRecord.lean 43450–43453),
which costs one more Toffoli on each side (`OneHotCornersDevelop.classify`
and `tagClassify` have 4 CCX; the record tag encoding has 3) and is not the
encoding expected by `AboveFieldPointDevelop.eraseB` / `loadB`.

`RecordMiddleEncoding` is the one-line structural repair: the hosted middle is
the record middle with the borrowed generic block replaced.  Once
`hostedMiddle` is defined with the record encoding it holds by `rfl`.
-/

section

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace ECDSAAdd.Entrant.StairMiddleShape

open ECDSAAdd Arithmetic Challenge
open MappedCompressed Secp256k1 BalancedField

def RecordMiddleEncoding : Prop :=
  ∀ (C : Point) (cx cy : Fp),
    StairConcreteAssembly.hostedMiddle C cx cy =
      AboveFieldPointDevelop.encode C ++ AboveFieldPointDevelop.eraseB ++
        StairConcreteAssembly.hostedBorrowGeneric cx cy ++
        AboveFieldPointDevelop.loadB ++ AboveFieldPointDevelop.decode C

end ECDSAAdd.Entrant.StairMiddleShape

end
end Merge_StairMiddleShape_at_Main

